Package: libpdfium8059
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: PDF rendering library (PDFium from Chromium)
 PDFium is the PDF engine of the Chromium project: it parses, renders and
 extracts text from PDF documents and supports annotations, forms, editing and
 saving through a C API.
 .
 This build is headless and server-oriented: the AGG renderer, no JavaScript
 (V8), no XFA forms and no Skia. It is built natively with Meson from the
 PDFium revision Chrome Stable ships (see sources.lock.json in the package
 documentation for the exact revision).
 .
 This package contains the shared library. The package name carries the ABI
 version (libpdfium.so.8059, introduced with Chromium branch 8059).

Package: libpdfium-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends:
 libpdfium8059 (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: PDF rendering library (PDFium from Chromium) - development files
 PDFium is the PDF engine of the Chromium project: it parses, renders and
 extracts text from PDF documents and supports annotations, forms, editing and
 saving through a C API.
 .
 This package contains the C headers (/usr/include/pdfium), the pkg-config
 file (pdfium.pc) and CMake package files (find_package(Pdfium), target
 Pdfium::pdfium).
